confidentially.","prediction":null},{"author":"PSF","created_at":"2026-06-26","text":"@(exmateriae) Yes, and frankly, I will probably go down again unless they get some kind of concrete good news (maybe hiring Dean Ball will help with that?).\n\nBasically, thanks perversely to the Trump admin trying to kill them, Anthropic has dominated the news and appears to have ensconced a perception that Open AI is \"next best\".\n\nPersonally, I think both should change CEOs to IPO, but neither will, and it also looks like Sam has more baggage than Dario (the Musk trial made it pretty clear that he will say whatever his audience wants to hear, which can be a great attribute for VC but a disaster for a listed co!).&#x20;","prediction":null},{"author":"Jgalt","created_at":"2026-06-26","text":"An OpenAI IPO this year has dropped to 25% [on Polymarket](https://polymarket.com/event/openai-ipo-by)\n\n![](https://cdn.metaculus.com/user_uploaded/HLuZFyfWoAAj5S0.jpg)","prediction":null},{"author":"exmateriae","created_at":"2026-06-26","text":"@(PSF) That's a good counterpoint, went down with Jgalt's post, especially the part where they didn't expect SPX to go down from 200...&#x20;","prediction":null},{"author":"exmateriae","created_at":"2026-06-26","text":"ootch this one might hurt in the ACX... Still think the community was too low at 35% but I might have been too high. One thing though, how could they be surprised that SpaceX stock went down after going very high? That was not certain but that always was a real possibility.","prediction":null},{"author":"PSF","created_at":"2026-06-26","text":"@(exmateriae)Yes but is he going to want to price below Anthropic?","prediction":null},{"author":"Jgalt","created_at":"2026-06-25","text":"New York Times: [OpenAI Leans Toward Waiting Until Next Year for I.P.O.](https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/25/technology/openai-ipo-artificial-intelligence.html)\n\n> OpenAI is leaning toward holding off its initial public offering until next year, three people involved in the company’s deliberations said, a turnabout that punctuates the uncertain future for fast-rising artificial intelligence giants.\n\n> The maker of ChatGPT hired bankers and lawyers with an eye toward a public offering as soon as the third or fourth quarter of this year, the people said. Sam Altman, the company’s chief executive, pushed those advisers to find a way for the start-up to be valued at $1 trillion, up from the company’s last private valuation of \n> &#x20;\n> [$730 billion](https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/31/technology/openai-12-billion-latest-funding-round.html)\n> &#x20;\n> , according to the people involved, who did not want to be named because they were not permitted to speak publicly about internal deliberations.\n\n> But a cascade of recent developments has caused OpenAI’s executives to shift away from their most aggressive aspirations. Top of mind is what has happened to Elon Musk’s SpaceX after its I.P.O. this month. It was the largest ever, raising more than $85 billion and reaching a valuation of $1.77 trillion on its debut. Since then, SpaceX’s stock has been on a downward slide, as shares slumped to $153 at the end of the trading day on Thursday after reaching a high of $202 last week.","prediction":null},{"author":"exmateriae","created_at":"2026-06-10","text":"@(MaxA) Interesting, although I wouldn't trust Altman in most contexts, I think he's gonna want to counter Anthropic's IPO and he shouldn't wait too much.&#x20;","prediction":null},{"author":"MaxA","created_at":"2026-06-10","text":"The community has likely overreacted to the filing news:\n\n[https://archive.is/fN2pg](https://archive.is/fN2pg)\n\n\"Sam Altman told staff in a Slack message on Monday that he expects OpenAI to go public “within the next year” and that “many things could cause it to be sooner or later in that range, but filing now gives us optionality if we want to go sooner.”","prediction":null}]}
